# Editor and OS noise
*~
*.swp
.idea
.vs
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode, wherever it lands
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Node's install tree, and everything the three packages compile or bundle into:
# `dist` is core's and shell's JavaScript and ui's built renderer, `dist-types` is
# the declarations ui emits so `tsc -b` can span all three, and the buildinfo files
# are the incremental state that makes a second typecheck cheap.
node_modules/
dist/
dist-types/
*.tsbuildinfo

# `npm run shots` writes its pictures and their index here (RG209): a reading of this tree
# for whoever changed it, regenerated on demand and true of no other clone.
.shots/

# Vitest Browser Mode writes a screenshot of the page here for every failed layout test (RG213),
# and `failures/` is what a red run keeps of itself (RG232). Both are evidence about one run on
# one machine: read after it, regenerated by the next, and true of no other clone.
.vitest/

# Electron Builder's output. RG46 is the task that configures it; the directory is
# named here so a local packaging experiment cannot be committed by accident.
release/

# roadkeep's own working directory: lint reports and run state, regenerated on
# demand and never read by another clone. Also where `roadkeep install --vendor`
# puts a pinned engine, which is this checkout's choice and not the repo's.
.roadkeep/

# Claude Code's project directory is local state except for the files roadkeep
# needs a clone to carry: settings.json declares the marketplace and enables the
# plugin, hooks/ holds the launcher that gives Claude Code on the web (which has
# no `/plugin`) the same guard a local machine gets from the plugin, and skills/
# is the copy `roadkeep install` keeps in step.
#
# agents/ joins them for the same reason skills/ is here: the /audit flow is a skill
# that dispatches two subagent definitions, and a clone missing them has a skill that
# names agents nobody on that machine has.
#
# settings.local.json is deliberately NOT un-ignored: it carries this machine's
# permission mode and absolute memory paths, which are true of nobody else's clone.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/hooks/
!/.claude/skills/
!/.claude/agents/

# Python's bytecode cache under hooks/. `!/.claude/hooks/` un-ignores that directory,
# so the generic `__pycache__/` rule above no longer reaches it — a hook the interpreter
# has imported once would otherwise leave a .pyc beside it that `git add -A` commits.
/.claude/hooks/__pycache__/
